From: Kudos Cards <tech@kudoscards.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:00:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Refuse background artwork that cannot print, at upload
 and at save

- shared-types/card-artwork: backgroundArtworkVerdict (shape + pixels, one
  rule for ours and the customer's), orientedPixelSize (EXIF), elementDistortion,
  customArtworkDocument, newMemberBackgroundUrls
- API: ArtworkGateService measures a member's new background at the save
  (SavedDesignsService.parseDocument), allowlisted to our storage host,
  fail-open on infrastructure, refused on artwork
- Web: 'Upload your own artwork' builds a full-bleed background instead of a
  450x600 element (which left an 8mm strip and stretched every upload to 3:4);
  both background uploads are measured and refused before a byte is sent;
  image elements warn when stretched out of shape, with a one-click fix
- docs/card-artwork-print-integrity.md: findings, decisions, remaining phases

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
