From: Kudos Cards <tech@kudoscards.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:11:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Print for the printer in the room: folded A5 sheets,
 borderless overhang, printed footer

The cards are printed on a Canon imagePROGRAF PRO-310 onto A5 blanks folded
to A6. The engine emitted one A6 face per page and left the imposition to the
driver, on a printer that has no borderless A6 at all.

- print-pdf: sheetGeometry + renderCardsPdf. 'folded-sheet' lays the outside
  (back | front) and inside (inside-left | inside-right) on a landscape sheet
  twice the trim width, in manual-duplex order. borderlessExtensionMm models
  the driver's enlargement so the trim lands on the paper edge after it.
  backFooter 'print' draws the reserved strip (QR, caption, logo) in-house.
- shared-types/print-profile: the house setup as one setting; PrintProfile
  service/module, GET/PUT /admin/print/profile, 'Print setup' admin panel.
- print run: reads the profile; per-run layout/footer overrides in the
  overlay and DTO; the calibrated extension is never a per-run choice.
- docs/card-artwork-print-integrity.md: D8-D10 and the re-ordered phases.

