+## The printer, and what it changes
+
+The cards are printed in-house on a **Canon imagePROGRAF PRO-310** onto **A5
+300gsm card blanks** that fold to A6. That is not the setup the print engine
+was written for — it emits one A6 face per page at exact trim, which the
+driver then has to impose two-up onto the A5 sheet, and the PRO-310 has no A6
+in its borderless size list at all (A5 is there; custom sizes cannot be
+borderless). Three things follow, and the engine now does all three:
+
+**D8 — The engine imposes the sheet; the driver does not.** `folded-sheet`
+layout (`sheetGeometry`, `renderCardsPdf`): per card, page 1 is the outside
+(back | front) and page 2 the inside (inside-left | inside-right) on one
+landscape sheet twice the trim width — 210 × 148 for A6, which is A5, the size
+the printer _does_ print borderless. The order is exactly what the driver's
+manual duplex wants (odd pages, reload, even pages). A front-only design still
+gets a blank inside sheet so it folds into a card. `face-per-page` stays as a
+layout for anyone who needs it.
+
+**D9 — Borderless overhang is modelled, not hoped away.** A borderless driver
+does not print to the edge; it _enlarges the page_ and lets the overhang fall
+off the paper (Canon: "the printed image is enlarged to fill the whole page …
+slight cropping may occur at the edges"). Nothing outside the PDF's page box
+ever reaches the driver, so bleed cannot be added _around_ the page. Instead
+`borderlessExtensionMm` — read off a calibration print and stored in the print
+profile — makes the engine draw each card fractionally smaller and centred, so
+that after the printer's scaling the trim lands on the paper edge and what is
+cut off is background. Pinned by test: scale the page about its centre by the
+printer's factor and the trim's outer edge lands at exactly 0.
+
+**D10 — The back strip can be ours to print.** The stock is blank and the QR is
+printed in-house, so `backFooter: "print"` draws the reserved 30mm itself — a
+white band over whatever the customer put there (the same rule as clipping),
+this card's QR, a caption, and the logo — in the same pass as the artwork, so
+it is always in register. `reserved` (clip) stays for pre-printed stock and
+for a QR batch done out of house.
+
+All three live in one **print profile** (`shared-types/print-profile.ts`,
+`PrintProfileService`, `PUT /admin/print/profile`, the "Print setup" panel):
+layout, back footer, borderless extension. Layout and footer can be switched
+per run in the print overlay; the extension cannot — it describes the printer.
 
